    "body": "This pull request adds custom-unit integration coverage to CI by teaching `scripts/test-integration.sh` to run mintd with `sat` plus a requested custom unit, then wiring custom-unit runs into the core and adapter integration workflows.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe multi-unit branch exercised the existing sat integration path, but CI did not run the shared adapter harness against a non-sat mint unit. That left custom-unit mint, send, receive, melt, sweep, and payment-request paths dependent on local/manual coverage.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Add `--custom-unit UNIT` support to `scripts/test-integration.sh`, including mintd config generation, unit normalization, env propagation, and cleanup.\n- Thread `customUnit` through the shared adapter integration harness so balances, send amounts, melt quotes, sweep calls, P2PK flows, and payment requests stay scoped to the selected unit.\n- Add custom-unit integration jobs for core, indexeddb, expo-sqlite, sqlite-bun, and sqlite3 workflows.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `bun run --filter='@cashu/coco-adapter-tests' build`\n- `bun run --filter='@cashu/coco-core' typecheck`\n- `bun run --filter='@cashu/coco-adapter-tests' typecheck`\n- `bun run --filter='@cashu/coco-core' test:unit`\n- `./scripts/test-integration.sh core --custom-unit usd -t 'custom-unit tokens'`\n\n## Changeset\n\n- Covered by the existing multi-unit major changeset: `.changeset/fresh-amounts-arrive.md`. No separate changeset was added for this CI/test-harness coverage commit.",
